# CC's sqrt, as Sage's ComplexNumber.sqrt: on the real line sqrt(x), or
# sqrt(-x) I for x < 0 (an exact 0 real part on the negative axis); else
# a = sqrt((|z| + x)/2) and b = y/a/2, from -z where x < 0 and |y| < |x|,
# |z| correctly rounded (mpfr_hypot).  Not the power z^(1/2), exp(log(z)/2).
# The parts are printed in hex, the operands written in hex.
rows = [
    (float.fromhex('-0x1.0000000000000p+0'), float.fromhex('0x0.0p+0')),
